    "done_when": "The manifest lists every caller of routing._repository_tree_snapshot and routing._tree_state with the entry point that reaches it. At the base these are dispatch.py:5061, dispatch.py:6835, promotion.py:2233, promotion.py:4162 and routing.py:578. tests/test_boundary_check_reads_two_trees.py passes under the root .venv python. It uses a temporary repository with 50 registered worktrees and a git shim on PATH that counts status calls, and it drives the crew complete entry point. A fenced run's snapshot holds 2 trees, its own worktree and the main checkout, and its promotion makes 2 status calls. An unfenced run's snapshot holds 51 trees, and its promotion makes 51. With the same shim, one dispatch of a fenced run makes at most 2 status calls for that run. The run record carries whether the fence was composed, and promotion reads that recorded fact, not the current default. A run recorded before this change, with no such field, keeps the full scan. A fenced run whose worker wrote into the main checkout is still refused at promotion, and the refusal names that tree. The declared negative control is executed and logged. The test files importing reckon.crew.routing, reckon.crew.promotion or reckon.crew.dispatch show 0 added failures between a base arm and a head arm, run with pytest-xdist -n 8, each arm with its own --basetemp under /tmp deleted afterwards. Stop and log the df reading if /tmp has under 5 GB free. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and command and ending EXIT=.",
